Z||000000||Scratchy||11-10-1999||01:56 PM||||First of all, hello to all as I'm new here...<P>While browsing the archives I found a project by Darklord (if I remember) of creating a clutchless system à la Ferrari...I also had this idea a couple months ago and while looking for info on existing products I found this:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.accessunlimited.com/drivematic/overview.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.accessunlimited.com/drivematic/overview.html</A> <P>I'll Email them for more info...and of course keep you posted...<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Bens88GT||11-10-1999||11:27 PM||||Wow! That place that makes this "Drive-matic" is only about 2 miles from my apartment! I didn't think there was anything interesting out here in Binghamton. I'll give them a call sometime soon and maybe drop by to look at their automatic clutch and how it works. I'll ask them about the possibility of using it with a Fiero and post what they tell me here.||||reg||3
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-11-1999||01:39 AM||||cool!<P>The system I have in mind is a bit different than that. Currently the planned system uses an automatic shifter knob, from a cavalier or something similar, but on a manual trans shifter rod with a hole drilled through the center for wires. when the shifter button is pressed, it applies power to a big solenoid which engages the clutch. when you let go of the button after shifting, the clutch disengages and you hit the accelerator again.<P>be sure to let us know what you find out about this company, their system sounds pretty cool.<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 11-11-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Scratchy||11-22-1999||09:28 PM||||Well, bad news...unless you can afford to have a Lambo, you probably would do a very bad move of having it installed on a fiero...cost is over 10k $...about the same cost as the F1 transmission option on the Ferrari...their is system is top notch though...but due to a limited market...price are high to cover the extensive R&D or so I was told...anything on your side?<P>But I have eyed another similar option...more soon, I hope.||||reg||1
